#!/bin/sh
exec 2>&1
# Fail closed: while /etc/nftables.conf exists but no ruleset is loaded, no
# interface comes up. Once 'nft -f /etc/nftables.conf' succeeds, this carries
# on by itself at the next check.
if [ -f /etc/nftables.conf ] && [ -z "$(nft list ruleset 2>/dev/null)" ]; then
    echo "no firewall ruleset is loaded; not bringing the network up"
    exec sleep 30
fi
for dev in /sys/class/net/*; do
    name=${dev##*/}
    [ "$(cat "$dev/type" 2>/dev/null)" = 1 ] || continue
    ip link set "$name" up
    # shellcheck disable=SC2093
    exec udhcpc -f -i "$name"
done
exec sleep 10
